*combine* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

Chip's build system

Bundles multiple ChipLang source files into a single program based on the configuration in ''combine.chp''.
Binary bundles (''.chipbin'') are standalone executables with embedded files and plugins.
Text bundles (''.chh'') are libraries that can be loaded by other programs.

*Usage:*
- ''chippy combine'' - Process default ''combine.chp'' configuration
- ''chippy combine path/to/config.chp'' - Process specific configuration file
- ''chippy combine new'' - Generate new template ''combine.chp'' file

*Configuration:*
- ''Project'': Output program name
- ''Version'': Program version string
- ''Licence'': Path to license file to include
- ''Output'': Output executable filename
- ''Source'': Main source file entry point
- ''Paths'': List of directories to search for dependencies
- ''PluginPaths'': List of directories to search for plugins
- ''Assets'': List of asset files to bundle
- ''External'': List of dependencies combine shouldn't bundle and just keep as loads
- ''ExternalPlugins'': List of plugins combine shouldn't bundle and just keep as ploads
- ''StripComments'': Remove comments from bundled output
- ''StripWhitespace'': Remove excess whitespace from bundled output
- ''ProduceBundle'': Create binary bundle (''true'') or text bundle (''false'')

*Features:*
- Automatic dependency resolution via ''load()'' statements
- Automatic plugin collection via ''pload()'' statements
	- only with ''ProduceBundle == true''
- Circular dependency prevention
- Licence header insertion (when configured)
- Comment/whitespace stripping (when configured)
- Safety checks:
	- Symbol collision detection in file scope (see ''chippy doc scoping'')
	- Syntax error detection

*Bundle Types:*
- *Binary bundle*: Standalone executable with embedded assets and plugins.
  This is recommended when using plugins or bundled assets in your program.

- *Text bundle*: Multiple Chip source files combined into one text-file
  This is recommended when your program uses no plugins or relies on no bundled assets.

*Returns:*
- Exit code 0 on success, non-zero on failure
